A||||4||falconhulk||squeaky sunroof||||1||
Z||000000||falconhulk||11-28-2001||10:17 AM||||I used rubber rejuvanator on all my gaskets and rubber  pieces about 1 month ago.  Since then my sunroof squeaks.  I have tightened everything.  it does not squeak while up just in the doen position.   Anyone have any ideas?  Its driving me crazy!  Its like a creaking noise or squeaking.||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-28-2001||10:21 AM||||I find vaseline works great on sunroofs...makes the rubber all soft again.. I have been using it on my cars sunroofs/tbars for the last 10-15 years with no problems.<P>I keep a small package handy for the door rubbers in the winter.. better then a froze door rubber  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||11-28-2001||12:23 PM||||try taking out the glass and giving the locating tabs in the glass panel a slight bend up ( CAREFULLY ) - this will put a sealing load back on the gasket<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||anatodigit||11-28-2001||03:09 PM||||this is what i did to mine   ..undo the handle like as if you were going to take the glass out     and put grease on the two knobs that hold the handle into the base. then put it back together.   That fixed up the squeeks and creeks on mine||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-28-2001||06:28 PM||||Another thing to rejuventate rubber parts is Lemon Extract -- gets the seals clean and rejuventates the rubber at the same time. Tightening the hinges and latch will definitely help - the squeeking is caused by the glass moving around slightly on the rubber seals.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
